  "question": {
    "text": "The term that corrects for the attractive forces present in a real gas in the van der Waals' equation is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wjDGk",
      "text": "\n$n b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Wy6n8",
      "text": "\n$n^2 a / V^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sFrhm",
      "text": "\n$-\\left(n^2 a / V^2\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2cGxX",
      "text": "\n$-n b$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In the van der Waals' equation\n$$\n\\left(p+\\frac{n^2 a}{V^2}\\right)(V-n b)=n R T\n$$\nThe pressure correction factor $\\left(n^2 a / V^2\\right)$ accounts for intermolecular attraction in real gas.",
    "image": null
  },
